# Network and I/O

- Treat every remote byte, header, frame, status, redirect, and length as
  untrusted.
- Bound message size, buffering, decompression, concurrency, retries, and total
  elapsed time.
- Handle partial reads and writes, disconnects, duplicate delivery, reordering,
  timeout, cancellation, and protocol-version mismatch.
- Make retryable mutations idempotent or attach a stable idempotency key.
- Validate certificates, host identity, authentication, authorization, and
  redirect boundaries using established libraries.
- Do not log secrets or sensitive payloads.
- Test fragmented input, malformed framing, slow peers, dependency failure, and
  clean resource release.
